{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652019-are-our-players-trolling-each-other","id":652019,"title":"Are our players trolling each other?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-04T20:03:01-07:00","id":652019,"title":"Are our players trolling each other?","content":"The Chronicle I've been playing is coming to a really tense point.<br /> <br /> The pre-Chronicle plot was that the Lancea et Sanctum controlled the city for most of history, and the bulk to the Sanctified leadership were killed in a Carthian-lead revolution. The Carthians, with support from a small number of Drakes, established a &quot;church of reason&quot; and forbid the practice of Blood Sorcery and worship of Longinus or the Crone.<br /> <br /> Our Coterie consisted of two &quot;Renouncers&quot; (former Sanctified) one Invictus playing for which ever side she thought would gain advantage, and Drake who supported the Carthians. The Drake's sire was the head of the &quot;church of reason&quot; if you find that important.<br /> <br /> The revolutionaries proved rather ineffective at keeping the City in order. Our Coterie was put in charge of imposing feeding restrictions. In one of our early sessions, we encountered a Strix possessing a corpse that had been drained by another Kindred, who seemed to have an interest in our Coterie.<br /> <br /> After locating the offender who killed a mortal they weren't &quot;supposed' to feed from, the Invictus in our coterie decided to execute him as a warning to the rest of the Kindred in the city.<br /> <br /> A high-ranking Carthian took insult to that effect (said Kindred was one of her underlings) and the ex-Sanctified characters were framed for &quot; wanton feeding&quot; resulting in Revenants rising.<br /> <br /> We were able to prove our innocence, and the Renouncers survived, but we were tasked with finding the source of the Revenants.<br /> <br /> At that point we were approached by Striges again, who informed us that they would help us survive an upcoming crisis--and implied that they would do so by helping us commit Diablerie.<br /> <br /> My character--one of the Sanctified &quot;Renouncers&quot; who still kept the faith--decided at that point that the Striges were not to be trusted under any circumstance. Part of his &quot;belief&quot; (and subsequent character arc) was that his faith was the only thing keeping his hold on Humanity and Diablerie was the one line he could never cross, lest he become a monster.<br /> <br /> The Invictus thought differently--the Strix were the only ones that offered to help us, and accepted a favor to call in later.<br /> <br /> We went after the Revenants, and we were trying to interrogate one to lead us back to where it came from (a Kindred seemed responsible) but the Invictus got impatient and called on the Strix to posses the Revenant.<br /> <br /> My character--who now thinks the Strix are pure evil and want us to eat souls--declared he would not let the Stix touch the Revenant. After a tense stand off, my character ended up Embracing the Revenant.<br /> <br /> The Strix was pleased at that (we figured out any action that decreases Humanity pleases this particular Strix) and left. <br /> <br /> At that point, the Invictus declared she was leaving the Coterie...and this is where my question comes in.<br /> <br /> My character had been causing trouble most of the game--due to bad interactions with Kine (he&quot;s a Nosferatu), ruffling the feathes of the Carthians in charge, and a failed roll to resist Frenzy that resulted in him attacking the sheriff... I acknowledge that my character, with his illegitimate Embrace, has now crossed the line between asset and liability. <br /> <br /> But the other two players tried to convince the Invictus character to kill or betray my character in order to keep the Invictus in the Coterie. I offered to play my new Childe to keep things going, or even take over playing the Strix, but the Invictus's player declined. <br /> <br /> So now our Storyteller had to come up with something for the Invictus character to do whilr we pursue the main plot. I'm not mad at the player. Everyone was acting in character. But it still kind of feels like bad behavior on one of our parts--we both put each other in situations where we wouldn't back down. My character hated Strix, the Invictus player believed they were our salvation.<br /> <br /> Splitting the Coterie seems like an unnecessary burden on the ST...I'm just wondering how other players of STs would have handled the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7033,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7033-funsize","user":"FunSize","date":". 09-04-2015, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7033-funsize","name":"FunSize","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T20:22:28-07:00","id":652046,"title":"","content":"That all seems perfectly reasonable to me. Requiem is not D&amp;D, and &quot;never split the party&quot; is about the worst possible advice for a Requiem ST. Also, I assume by &quot;Drakes&quot; you mean the Ordo Dracul? Their nickname is usuall Dragons, not Drakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T21:36:28-07:00","id":652094,"title":"","content":"Tl;DR sounds like your group needs to have a serious out of game discussion about these issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T07:46:57-07:00","id":652474,"title":"","content":"Backstabbing isa thing in vampire. The game is working as intended, from the sounds of it. I'd just say keep playing, and if your character dies, or something else happens, then go from there. Make a new one. <br /> <br /> Its important to keep things OOC and IC separate, because you can get really vicious in this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-05-2015, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T08:36:23-07:00","id":652609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652019-are-our-players-trolling-each-other?p=652046#post652046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That all seems perfectly reasonable to me. Requiem is not D&amp;D, and &quot;never split the party&quot; is about the worst possible advice for a Requiem ST. Also, I assume by &quot;Drakes&quot; you mean the Ordo Dracul? Their nickname is usuall Dragons, not Drakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious why the other two are siding wih someone interested in diablorie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T08:54:54-07:00","id":652648,"title":"","content":"I dpn't see any problem in all of t. I think it's all perfectly in character and reflects perfectly the political danse macabre of the Kindred. My only advice, as MCN said, is keeping IC and OOC feelings separate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T16:04:49-07:00","id":653122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652019-are-our-players-trolling-each-other?p=652609#post652609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious why the other two are siding wih someone interested in diablorie?</div> </div> </div> </div> Completely viable character for vampire chronicles. In fact, I encourage the tempation of diablarie.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T16:40:54-07:00","id":653143,"title":"","content":"The other Renouncer and the Dragon stayed with me and my new Childe, but the future of our Coterie is still up in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7033-funsize","name":"FunSize","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T19:08:45-07:00","id":653382,"title":"","content":"Considering they suggested that the Invictus character should kill your character, your character has dragged their reputations through the mud, and your character just made them accessories to an illicit embrace, a crime that you supposedly narrowly avoided execution for in the first place, I wouldn't bet money on your character's long term survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T20:02:41-07:00","id":653428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652019-are-our-players-trolling-each-other?p=653122#post653122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Completely viable character for vampire chronicles. In fact, I encourage the tempation of diablarie.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In 2e, there seems to be no temptation. Auspex can tell if you've done it. You risk final death if you're discovered. It's considered an evil worse than any crime any mortal could ever commit. You get your victim stuck in your head causing you problems for an exceedingly lengthy period of time unless you permanently scar yourself repeatedly. You risk addiction. You risk losing Humanity. All for a single dot in a Discipline and probably a fraction of a dot of Blood Potency. A full dot for an Elder. Two for an Ancient. (I know BP does not equal age, but I'm trying to be concise) Either of those coming with consequences far above and beyond the scope of this post. I can't see how anyone would see those drawbacks as worth the tiny reward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:55:33-07:00","id":653499,"title":"","content":"While Auspex can tell, it does require them to specifically target you and ask.<br /> <br /> But yes, it's sort of a losing game unless you specifically hunt elders, or go after folks with rarer disciplines. You'll likely lose Humanity while doing it, and while the costs of Humanity and Blood Potency have been decreased you don't want to be trading in 1 Humanity for .2 Blood Potency. Of course that's just a mechanical way of looking at it. In-game, diablerie is an easy path to power for vampires who don't particularly think much of vampires other than themselves and diablerie addiction can throw all reason out the window.<br /> <br /> In the end it shares the standard 'dark side' risk, and diablerists are either going to end up spiraling completely out of control and becoming draugr until they're hunted down, or be so cunningly in control you'll never see the threat until it's draining your hearts blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-06-2015, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T23:31:28-07:00","id":653537,"title":"","content":"Not taking away from other drawbacks, but Auspex isn't proof of anything. The Auspex user can tell, but everyone else has to take their word for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T03:51:25-07:00","id":653691,"title":"","content":"Humanity is only 2 experiences per dot, so mathematically speaking it's always profitable to commit diablerie on anyone of blood potency 3 or greater. Also I'm pretty sure you can take a bane for it, so there's that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T10:01:35-07:00","id":654042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652019-are-our-players-trolling-each-other?p=653691#post653691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also I'm pretty sure you can take a bane for it, so there's that too.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends how literally you take, 'Diablerie is always a breaking point, regardless of the vampire\u2019s Humanity score.' And whether or not you also make them roll for Impassioned Violence or Premeditated or Impassioned Killing, in which case you might have to take multiple banes in order to avoid a swifter degeneration, as each bane gives you a penalty to resisting further Humanity loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T10:15:07-07:00","id":654059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652019-are-our-players-trolling-each-other?p=653691#post653691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure you can take a bane for it, so there's that too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From the FAQ:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">What breaking point level is diablerie? Can it be overcome with a bane?</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Diablerie is a Humanity 1 breaking point. It can\u2019t be overcome with a bane.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T10:51:05-07:00","id":654086,"title":"","content":"I stand corrected. <br /> <br /> Still, I neglected to factor in the discipline/skill dot when I made that post, so the <i>least</i> a vamp can get out of diablerie is 3 experiences worth of stuff. More realistically you're looking at between 4 and 7 at the low end, to potentially 14 experiences at the top. That's enough to put you on the cusp of ancilla, going by the chart on page 82. Worth a humanity dot? I think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T11:03:34-07:00","id":654091,"title":"","content":"Ah, that was the line.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the addiction is automatic. It's not a matter of just finding one lone ancient and draining him dry and going on with the rest of your requiem like nothing ever happened. After that, you have to roll to resist any reasonable opportunity to commit diablerie, with a penalty based on the target's Blood Potency. So if you shared a haven with fellow coterie members, and one of them has commit diablerie, your potential for immortality is now determined by the willingness of your roommate to not get free stuff by killing you. And that's just ignoring the difficulty of being able to commit the act. Many vampires will wake up upon being attacked and put up a fight, and diablerie can be a huge suck on willpower. My players failed on following through with the act a few times.<br /> <br /> It's certainly an option to take. I think it would be more tempting to nomads and outsiders, or vampires who have made pacts with other beings to get around the drawbacks. But if it isn't, providing the diablerist has enough sway, they can shrug off accusations of the act. Prince Maxwell told his entire court he commit diablerie and basically told them they wouldn't do anything to him because the alternatives to him as a ruler would be detrimental to them.<br /> <br /> I really enjoy the whole diablerie concept, but I can appreciate why others would not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-06-2015, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T11:05:29-07:00","id":654094,"title":"","content":"More tangibly speaking, that's 1-3 months worth of experience, assuming one session per week and an average of 1 experience per session. And what's the drawback again? Upping the stakes and adding drama to the story? Sign me up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}